                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b] Target Audience: [/b] [I]   Those desperate for puzzles, really desperate. [/i]\n\n[b] Summary: [/b]  \n\nA disappointment from the get go. 101 Ways to Die found a 101 ways to annoy me with its implementation: in particular with the execution of the world's rules and attempting to complement it's puzzle game roots. When you're unsure of whether not a solution will work because you're unsure of whether or not the rules have changed, you've got a slight problem. And that's 101 ways in a nutshell. Setting up a bumper to launch a Splatt would be great, if the line that was shown for its path of flight was accurate to what truly happened. Guess what, it isn't. Sometimes, you complete objectives without understanding what exactly you did to do them. And the sad thing is, the core of the game and its concept is a good idea, it's just executed poorly here. There's just better games in the genre that does the same thing, and doesn't make you want to rip your hair out while doing it. \n\n[b]Gameplay Footage and Video Review:  https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XaH365x-oAw[/b] \n\n[u] Lists: [/u]\n[b]Positives:[/b]\n[list]\n[*] When the game allows for more open areas and more creativity on puzzles, you can get what the game is going for.\n[*] Playing pinball with one of the splats was the highlight of the game. When the game becomes chaotic, you can get a good laugh out of it.\n[*] Visuals once in a while do the job, especially on the replay close ups.\n[/list]\n\n[b]Negatives:[/b]\n[list]\n[*] A set of rules that don't seem to be consistent. It leads to frustration as you don't know what to expect.\n[*] Trial and Error gameplay in a bad way, due to not knowing the right type of information to complete a level.\n[*] UI feels uninspired, and sometimes gets in the way. Misleading instructions can lead to frustration. When you tell me to click on the tool, and I click on the actual tool, and it doesn't do anything, you can see why I'm sitting there going “WHAT DO YOU WANT FROM ME”. \n[*] Lacking visuals for certain elements (fan effects) that have in-game results.\n[*] Sound Design lacks oompf on kills and the results oft your mouse trap concoctions. \n[*] Weird controls for the PC platform. Backspace for cancel is just strange for me.\n[/list]\n\n[b] If you want more reviews/information regarding games I've reviewed, visit my curator. [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/6861768/]Dragnix Curator [/url][/b]",
